# DTF tier manifest: xff-authz-trust
#   (artifact-keeper #4681 / GHSA-59x8-r6jj-x95h, #4675, #4662; all in 1.11.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + sso.oidc-entra-shape, reused for its
# topology only: RATE_LIMIT_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=172.16.<slot>.64/28 on the mock
# network, so a throwaway curl container pinned to .70 is a TRUSTED proxy peer
# and one pinned to .90 is not; json-file log driver; mock-oidc doubles as the
# upstream of the Remotes below (its OIDC role is unused).
#
# THE BUGS
#   #4681  For a request whose TCP peer is a trusted proxy, the client IP
#          resolved from X-Forwarded-For was used for allowed_cidrs permission
#          conditions and audit-row IPs, although the backend cannot verify
#          the chain. Fixed: new XFF_TRUSTED_FOR_AUTHZ (default false); unset,
#          such a request has an UNKNOWN client IP for authz and audit
#          (IP-conditioned grants deny, audit rows record NULL) and startup
#          warns. A non-proxy peer still uses its TCP address.
#   #4675  The http_request span `uri` logged `ticket`, `X-Amz-Signature` and
#          other URL-carried credentials verbatim. Fixed: redacted, names
#          matched case-insensitively after percent-decoding (%74icket).
#   #4662  A Remote could be made public while carrying upstream credentials,
#          so anonymous callers spent them. Fixed: create, update and
#          PUT upstream-auth answer 400 PUBLIC_REMOTE_UPSTREAM_CREDENTIALS
#          unless allow_public_with_upstream_credentials is sent; responses
#          report public_with_upstream_credentials; the audit row records the
#          acceptance.
#
# TWO BOOTS, ONE COMPOSE PROJECT: phase 1 runs the profile as is (flag unset);
# phase 2 recreates ONLY the backend with XFF_TRUSTED_FOR_AUTHZ=true through a
# tier-local override (the qcmj-webhook-authz pattern), so `down -v` still
# reclaims everything.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: red on ak-backend:1.11.0 (10 FIX cases), green on 1.11.1 and
# on today's main. CONTROLS (green on both): an untrusted peer is judged by its
# TCP address for grants and audit; `token=` was already redacted (#544) and
# other parameters are logged unchanged; legitimate public / private Remote
# writes succeed; with XFF_TRUSTED_FOR_AUTHZ=true the forwarded address
# satisfies the grant and is recorded, and the warning is gone.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 calls back to back (exported by run.sh, so the
# phase-2 recreate keeps it).
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the Remote fetches mock-oidc on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem sso.oidc-entra-shape"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
